From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hdmitx: mute the video while Dolby Vision starts

When hdmi_current_eotf_type leaves EOTF_T_NULL, mute through vid_mute_op and
queue work_hdr_unmute, as the DRM path does for HDR10/HLG. A mode set clears
the packets and so re-arms the mute; the unmute stays tied to the first
trigger, hdr_mute_frame frames at the refresh rate current at that moment.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/media/vout/hdmitx20/hdmi_tx_main.c
+++ b/drivers/media/vout/hdmitx20/hdmi_tx_main.c
@@ -1007,6 +1007,12 @@
 	if (hdev->tx_comm.hdmi_current_eotf_type != type ||
 		hdev->tx_comm.hdmi_current_tunnel_mode != tunnel_mode ||
 		hdev->hdmi_current_signal_sdr != signal_sdr) {
+		if (hdr_mute_frame && hdev->tx_comm.hdmi_current_eotf_type == EOTF_T_NULL &&
+		    type != EOTF_T_NULL) {
+			hdmitx20_video_mute_op(0);
+			HDMITX_INFO("SDR->DV enter mute\n");
+			schedule_work(&hdev->work_hdr_unmute);
+		}
 		hdev->tx_comm.hdmi_current_eotf_type = type;
 		hdev->tx_comm.hdmi_current_tunnel_mode = tunnel_mode;
 		hdev->hdmi_current_signal_sdr = signal_sdr;
